sketch:
To make earth over again,—while I’m content
To make the pictures. Let me bring the sketch.
A tiptoe Danae, overbold and hot;

sketched:
That morning, in my London painting-room;
The face half-sketched, and slurred; the eyes alone!
But you ... you caught them up with yours, and said

skeered:
Dis worl' 's done puzzled me one w'ile;
I 's mighty skeered I 'll fall in doubt,
I des' won't try to reason out

skeert:
Den you stan' dah wond'rin',
Lookin' skeert an' stary;
I's a right to caper

skeart:
You 'd 'a' noticed in a glance
She was pow'rful shamed an' skeart;
But she looked so sweet an' peart,
